  "verdict": "With the rest of the dome at α 0.50 and the window at α_c 1.00 (the bound), no named window brings the capsule to the 70 °C EDLC rating — at most 58.9 °C, 61.8 °C with h_c × 0.7. The cambium under the flange's thinnest contact, in full sun and still air, stays under its 50 °C gate at the nominal h_c for one_package_in_the_crown_KXOB25-07X1TF, four_dies_in_the_crown_XOD17-04B, flat_crown_circle, and with h_c × 0.7 for one_package_in_the_crown_KXOB25-07X1TF, four_dies_in_the_crown_XOD17-04B; on the bound the largest dark aperture that keeps it under is 3.66 cm² at the nominal h_c and 1.65 cm² with h_c × 0.7 (floored; grid 0.10 cm²). Above those the bound does not clear the gate — which is not a crossing. Every number is an UPPER bound inherited from 71 and 78.",
  "not_seen": [
    "the window's optics — transmittance, its own absorption, the cavity's greenhouse (isothermal lump)",
    "a cell's real absorptance (α_c 0.90 is ours)",
    "the two cell-outline rows are LOWER bounds on the dark aperture: a window exposing the outline is at least as large — read them against the crossing",
    "the R5 edge: a window wider than the flat crown sits on it, and 71 models it as part of a flat disc — for every named window and every crossing (none wider than the bore) the beam term stays the bound (a centred convex patch, its edge sloping less than 90° − ψ* at the binding angle, projects as its planar disc), the diffuse term counts the planar disc, a few per cent less than the curved surface; grid points near the whole crown fall outside that condition, so no number at the grid's far end is cached",
    "71's own ceilings move the hot answer UP beyond these bounds: sunlit bark around the rim conducting in, ERA5 smoothing station maxima",
    "whether a window meets the ratified α ≤ 0.5 — a verdict, not a number",
    "the RF half of the window (01_03 §4)"
  ]
}
